\textbf{SUMMARY}
\par
\textbf{Decision analysis concepts and methciology have been demon-}
\par
\textbf{strated to have high potential for assisting defense declslon-}
\par
\textbf{makers. However, such assistance for defense executives can now}
\par
\textbf{be provided by only a few dozen professionals who have both the}
\par
\textbf{required technical competence and communication skills.}
\par
\textbf{Various computerized aids, such as the SRI computer programs}
\par
\textbf{for decision tree evaluation, facilitate the analysis of a decision}
\par
\textbf{problem; however, the existing software is useful only in the}
\par
\textbf{hands of a well-trained analyst or an exceptional executive. Fur-}
\par
\textbf{thermore, these programs only deal with a portion of the decision}
\par
\textbf{analysis process.}
\par
\textbf{We are engaged in the first year of a multi-year program}
\par
\textbf{to design a broad system of Integrated computer aids for decision-}
\par
\textbf{making that will foster the widespread application of decision}
\par
\textbf{analysis. This system encompasses all of the model building}
\par
\textbf{assessment, and analytical steps in the decision analysis proceed.}
\par
\textbf{In particular, the system augments the thought process of the}
\par
\textbf{user to describe the problem in convenient terms and to construct}
\par
\textbf{a useful decision model. In addition, the system permits assessing}
\par
\textbf{the information and preferences of the decision-maker or his dele-}
\par
\textbf{gates. Finally, the system determines the best course of action}
\par
\textbf{within the scope of the formulation and, by providing aids such}
\par
\textbf{as sensitivity analyses, gives the decision-maker insight into why}
\par
\textbf{that course of action was selected.}
