\textbf{1.1 Research Objectives}
\par
\textbf{The advantage to decision makers of having guidance in the}
\par
\textbf{analysis of decision problems has been amply demonstrated by cases}
\par
\textbf{where the time and resources for analysis were readily available.}
\par
\textbf{However, the need for guidance in rapidly developing decision sit-}
\par
\textbf{uations and the shortage of trained analytical personnel mean that}
\par
\textbf{few decisions can receive the amount of analysis they deserve.}
\par
\textbf{The major hope in realizing the benefits of Insightful analysis}
\par
\textbf{lies in using the computer to assist the analytical process. The}
\par
\textbf{assistance would be helpful at all levels, from the original charac-}
\par
\textbf{terization of the problem by the decision maker to the sophisticated}
\par
\textbf{manipulation of a decision model by the analyst. If such decision}
\par
\textbf{aids were available, decision makers could use some of them alone}
\par
\textbf{to achieve the benefits of preliminary analysis in problems that}
\par
\textbf{now receive only intuitive treatment. Analysts in turn could}
\par
\textbf{provide analysis in depth in situations where they now have the}
\par
\textbf{time or resources for only initial consideration of important issues.}
\par
\textbf{The availability of effective aids could have an important}
\par
\textbf{effect not only on individual decisions, but on the style of decision-}
\par
\textbf{making. In our present world without eas:ly accessible decision}
\par
\textbf{aids, decision makers can make decisions intuitively without criticism,}
\par
\textbf{but they may be considerably, and unconsciously, limited in the}
\par
\textbf{size of the projects they will undertake or in their boldness of}
