\emph{Computational Graphs}
\par
\textbf{When operators and entities are linked together, either indi-}
\par
\textbf{vidually or through the use of operator rules, the result is a}
\par
\textbf{computational graph that specifies the structure of the model.}
\par
\textbf{These graphs can be used to specify any of the models used in de-}
\par
\textbf{cision analysis: decision trees, Markov processes, financial models,}
\par
\textbf{material flows over time, fault trees, etc. In fact, given the very}
\par
\textbf{basic nature of operators and entities, it is difficult to conceive}
\par
\textbf{of a model that cannot be put into the form of a computational}
\par
\textbf{graph. This is not to say that computational graphs are the most}
\par
\textbf{efficient way to model every decision problem, but rather that}
\par
\textbf{they are sufficiently important that they should be incorporated}
\par
\textbf{into any general modeling language.}
\par
