\textbf{gories is further subdivided until we reach the level w'\textasciicircum ere ex-}
\par
\textbf{perts are available to estimate the inputs to the model. The}
\par
\textbf{stopping point is a decision not an outcome. For example, if one}
\par
\textbf{of the costs is for crude oil in 1980, we can estimate it directly,}
\par
\textbf{or we can build a world energy model to predict the future price}
\par
\textbf{of crude oil.}
\par
\textbf{Figure 2.5 shows how top-down modeling is integrated into the}
\par
\textbf{decision analysis cycle. At the start of the >>roject intuition}
