\textbf{2.2.5 The Value of Flexibility}
\par
\textbf{The notion that a good decision strategy is a flexible one has}
\par
\textbf{long been intuitively appreciated by decision makers. Nearly every-}
\par
\textbf{one io familiar with a story of a plan that went wrong because it}
\par
\textbf{failed to adjust for some unforeseen circumstance. Decision analysis}
\par
\textbf{has had little to say on the subject of flexibility. However, recent}
\par
\textbf{research on the concept o: flexibility shows that this subject should be}
\par
\textbf{incorporated in a decision norphology.}
\par
\textbf{'{$<$}oughly speaking, something is flexible if it may be easily}
\par
\textbf{varied. However, in the context of decision making, ease of varia-}
\par
\textbf{tion may be described by many different characteristics, Our point}
\par
\textbf{of view is that the flexibility of a given decision variable is}
\par
\textbf{determined by the nature of the choice set associated with that var-}
\par
\textbf{iable. The lirger the choice set, the greater the decision flexi-}
\par
\textbf{bility. If the choice set consists of a single point element, In}
\par
\textbf{other words if the decision has already been committed, we say that}
\par
\textbf{the decision variable is inflexible.}
\par
\textbf{A number of the classical micro-economic decision problems}
\par
\textbf{for which flexibility is a concern may be treated within thif}
\par
\textbf{framework. Merkhofer (9] has shown that the problem of sizing a}
\par
\textbf{production facility can be so analyzed.* The decision strategy of}
\par
\textbf{committing something less than one's total resources so as to be}
\par
\textbf{prepared to meet unforeseen opportunities may also be expressed}
\par
\textbf{as a problem of maintaining flexibility.}
\par
\textbf{* For a discussion of this problem see Marschak and Nelson [8] and}
\par
