\textbf{3.2.1 CADMUS (Computer Aids for Decision Makers: User System)}
\par
\textbf{What follows is a tentative description of the operation of}
\par
\textbf{an interactive computer graphics system for decision making. We}
\par
\textbf{shall call this system CADMUS , an acronym for Computerized Aids}
\par
\textbf{for Decision Makers: User System. Although the characteristics}
\par
\textbf{which we ascribe to CADMUS are within the capabilities of present}
\par
\textbf{generation hardware and software technology, our objective is to}
\par
\textbf{communicate a perception of how such a system might usefully em-}
\par
\textbf{ploy branching structures as a language for model building. Our}
\par
\textbf{objective is not to define the detailed characteristics of such a}
\par
\textbf{system. Before we become lost in the particulars of designing}
\par
\textbf{computer systems, we need to improve further our understanding of}
\par
\textbf{the alternative ways of describing decision problems.}
