\textbf{3.4 CONCLUSIONS AND SUMMARY}
\par
\textbf{A branching structure has be\textasciicircum n described which allows a}
\par
\textbf{decision maker to express compactly the structure of a decision}
\par
\textbf{tiiublem. Although the technique was originally developed to}
\par
\textbf{describe single stage continuous deterministic models, we have}
\par
\textbf{seen th\textasciicircum t the method may be expanded so as to be used in sequen-}
\par
\textbf{tial problems with discrete events and significant uncertainties.}
\par
\textbf{The system described is an illustration of how a computerized}
\par
\textbf{graphical structure may help a decision maker to formulate a deci-}
\par
\textbf{sion problem. Current research has demonstrated the feasibility}
\par
\textbf{of such a system but additional research will be required to de-}
\par
\textbf{termine exact software specifications.}
